use ../../../lib/UiComponent

from ../../buttons/Button import Button

export ui-component QrCode:
    description:
        A QR code shows a piece of text, usually a web address, as a square
        pattern that a phone camera or scanner can read. It only shows
        information; it doesn't collect any.

    composes:
        - @{Button}

    value:
        The component gives it the text to show. When the text changes, the
        pattern is redrawn straight away. Longer text makes a denser pattern.

    errorCorrection:
        The component chooses how much of the pattern can be covered or
        damaged and still be read, from a little to about a third. More makes
        the pattern denser, but is needed when a logo covers the middle or the
        code may be printed small or get scuffed.

    logo:
        A small picture, such as a logo, can be placed in the middle. The code
        still reads as long as the error correction allows for what it
        covers.

    appearance:
        It stays sharp at any size. The colours of the pattern and its
        background can be chosen, but scanners need strong contrast between
        them, and a dark pattern on a light background is the safest.

    name:
        The pattern means nothing to someone who can't see or scan it. It has
        a name that assistive tools read out, saying what it's for, such as
        "QR code for the booking page". The text it holds isn't read out as
        part of the pattern; if people need it, such as a web address, the app
        shows it nearby as text or a Link.

    saving:
        The component can offer a Button that saves the code as an image,
        including any logo. Which image formats are offered is up to the
        chosen library.

    nonGoals:
        - No scanning. Reading codes with a camera is a separate component
        - Only QR codes, not other kinds of barcode
